From 37a4e91f1ebe92fb6f84a07b8a952b11a4afb84d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:14:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] arrange: carried bitsets up to 512 labels, each r1 at
 the words it needs

The carried path now runs up to CARRY_MAX_W = 8 words with W = ceil(L/64)
exactly (instantiations for 5-7 words; the matrix path is unchanged and
only used above 512 labels or without AVX-512BW), and each first row r1 is
searched with only the words up to its largest label (opts.r1_width, on by
default; bench --no-r1-width): the r1 run in runs of equal width, each
filling the depth-0 lists from its first r1 on. The adaptive cross state
carries across runs, so the nodes are exactly those of a single width.
Cross support builds its unions 4 words at a time (8 W accumulators did not
fit in registers above 4 words). -DR1_SAMPLE: env-driven r1 sampling by
global index with a per-r1 log.

Paired (same r1, thread CPU, vs fdb77fc): 2.84x at 13 7 4 3 1 1 S = 2650
(N 31.7k, 279 labels), 3.13x at S = 2500, 2.87x at 9 6 4 3 1 1 1 1 S = 2700,
2.18x in the V_d searches at S = 2650; 1.23x at S = 2200, 1.31x at
12 6 3 2 1 1 S = 1200, 1.00-1.09x elsewhere, prod.txt 1.004. Same squares
and hashes everywhere; fuzz_arrange mode 7 (257-500 labels) and width
variants, 0 fails on 2,000 fresh seeds. See research/ideas.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
